<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-19">19 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Ugolino di Conti is elected Pope Gregory IX</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Following the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii">Pope Honorius III</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-ix">Ugolino di Conti</a> was elected pope and took the name Gregory IX. He reigned until 1241 and is known for issuing the Decretales and instituting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medieval-inquisition">Papal Inquisition</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii">Pope Honorius III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-ii-of-denmark" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valdemar-ii-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-22">22 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">A north German coalition defeats Valdemar II at Bornhöved</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Bornhöved in Holstein, an army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a>, Dithmarschen, Holstein and north German nobles under Count Adolf IV of Schauenburg and Holstein defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-ii-of-denmark">Valdemar II of Denmark</a>. Valdemar lost most of his German conquests but kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-ii-of-denmark">Valdemar II of Denmark</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-18">18 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Genghis Khan dies during his campaign against the Tangut</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> died during the siege of the Western Xia, traditionally on this date. He had built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>, which under his heirs became the largest contiguous land empire in history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-29">29 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Pope Gregory IX excommunicates Emperor Frederick II</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Gregory IX excommunicated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a> for again delaying his promised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a>. Frederick went anyway, regaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> by treaty in 1229 and crowning himself in the Holy Sepulchre.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/leszek-the-white" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leszek-the-white.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-24">24 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Assassins kill High Duke Leszek the White at Gąsawa</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At a council of Polish Piast dukes near Gąsawa in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuyavia">Kuyavia</a>, attackers assassinated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leszek-the-white">Leszek the White</a>, High Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, and gravely wounded Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-bearded">Henry the Bearded</a> of Silesia. Henry survived to become High Duke of all Poland from 1232.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leszek-the-white">Leszek the White</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-bearded">Henry the Bearded</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuyavia">Kuyavia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bornhoved">Battle of Bornhöved</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Bornhöved was fought on 22 July 1227 in Holstein, where an alliance of north German princes, including Count Adolf IV of Holstein, Count Henry of Schwerin, the Archbishop of Bremen and the city of Lübeck, defeated King Valdemar II of Denmark.</p></div></li></ol></section>
